{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3301","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3301","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3301\",\"parent_revision\":\"4f919f8c1547d46543adad2c7cc11ba9dbcbf8ae\",\"root_revision\":\"eaf19578ed713b9dbe6083d7b948180ff8cb7ce26fb510aa711babbdb0b91194\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDuring #3151's quality-gate multi-perspective-review swarm (ephemeral plan P38ce5ead, GitHub-backed), `sam_task(action='claim')` returned `claimed: false` with a self-contradictory status message (\\\"not-started, not not-started\\\") on the first two attempts for task T4. A third attempt succeeded.\\n\\nRoot cause identified by the T4 agent: a transient GitHub API `403 Forbidden` (rate-limit/backoff) on the underlying `GET /repos/...` call, not an actual task-state conflict \u2014 the agent re-read the task's status directly and confirmed it stayed `not-started` throughout both failed attempts. The claim path is swallowing or misinterpreting the 403 and surfacing it to the caller as a state-conflict message instead of the real transient-API-error condition.\\n\\nThe same agent reported this pattern affected tasks T2, T3, and T4 in the same swarm run (per a peer's report, not independently re-verified by this session beyond T4).\\n\\nImpact: an agent or orchestrator seeing \\\"claimed: false, not-started (not not-started)\\\" has no way to distinguish \\\"someone else has this task\\\" (a real conflict, should back off) from \\\"transient network/API failure, retry\\\" (should just retry) \u2014 the current error message actively points at the wrong cause.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: the claim implementation should surface the underlying HTTP status/exception distinctly from a genuine state-precondition failure, so callers can retry on 403/5xx without the misleading conflict framing.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Quality vigilance concern from #3151's complete-implementation quality-gate cycle \u2014 reported by dh:reviewer-accessibility (task T4, plan P38ce5ead) during multi-perspective-review\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d1e4e98192a833f7e307ade73a28f3de21934b83b2562c9a2c1429bc2c147c18\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABReqULA\"}"}